Use Cases	Interrupts, worker sync	Session state, config, tools
Summary
Agent Orchestrator v2 uses clusters for:

Valkey Pub/Sub Cluster: Fast cross-worker interrupt signaling via ao:interrupt channel
Central Cache Service Cluster: Two-tier persistent cache (Valkey L1 + Glide L2) via HTTP REST API
Data moves between them via:

Valkey: Direct async Redis client for pub/sub (no HTTP)
Central Cache: HTTP client with mTLS + JWT auth, routing through CacheServiceClient
Key architectural decisions:

Separation of concerns: signaling vs storage
Three-tier caching: TTLCache (L0) → Valkey (L1) → Glide (L2)
Request-scoped context using Python contextvars
Automatic mTLS in non-dev environments
Multi-tenancy via instanceId scoping
