Complete Utterance Journey
User: "Reset my password"
    ↓
[1] REST API receives utterance
    ↓ Set request context (instance_id, conversation_id)
    ↓ Initialize cache client
    
[2] Fetch conversation history from Central Cache
    ↓ HTTP GET → Valkey (L1) → Glide (L2)
    ↓ Append current utterance
    
[3] Fetch skills/agents from Central Cache
    ↓ HTTP GET → skills cached during handshake
    
[4] Execute pipeline
    ↓ COMPACT_PLANNER → PLANNER1 → AGENT_EXECUTION
    ↓ Save state to Central Cache after each stage
    ↓ Stream tokens via SSE queue
    
[5] Tool execution (if needed)
    ↓ Invoke Glide tool
    ↓ Set async lock in Valkey
    ↓ Wait for callback
    
[6] Generate response
    ↓ Stream final message chunks
    
[7] Update conversation history
    ↓ HTTP POST → Central Cache → Valkey + Glide
    
[8] Send "done" SSE event
    ↓ Close stream
    ↓ Clear request context

[If user interrupts during execution]
    ↓ Publish to Valkey ao:interrupt channel
    ↓ Owning worker receives broadcast
    ↓ Cancel pipeline task
    ↓ Send interrupt SSE event
This flow shows how every utterance interacts with both clusters multiple times throughout its lifecycle, with Valkey providing fast coordination and Central Cache Service providing persistent storage backed by ServiceNow Glide.

